  "result": "Perfect! All 86 tests pass. I've successfully added line discount support:\n\n**Updates to `src/errors.js`:**\n- Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error code\n\n**Updates to `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n1. **`createInvoice` now accepts `discountPercent`**:\n   - Each line can include `discountPercent` (0-100, decimals allowed)\n   - Defaults to 0 if omitted\n   - Validates range and type, returns `DISCOUNT_INVALID` if invalid\n\n2. **`addLine` now accepts `discountPercent`**:\n   - Same validation as `createInvoice`\n   - Defaults to 0 if omitted\n\n3. **New `lineDiscount(line)` function**:\n   - Calculates discount as `lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent / 100`\n   - Rounds with `roundCents()` for fractional cents\n   - Clamps result at 0 (no negative discounts)\n\n4. **`invoiceTotals` now returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }`**:\n   - `subtotal`: sum of all line totals\n   - `discount`: sum of all line discounts (each rounded)\n   - `total`: subtotal - discount, clamped at 0\n   - Example: line of 5 \u00d7 \u20ac95 with 10% discount = \u20ac475 - \u20ac47.50 = \u20ac427.50\n\n**13 new tests** covering:\n- Discount validation (ranges, types, decimals like 12.5)\n- Discount calculations on single and multiple lines\n- Clamping total at 0 when discount exceeds subtotal\n- Integration with `addLine` and `createInvoice`\n\nSample calculation verified:\n- 5 hours @ \u20ac95 (10% off) + 1 logo @ \u20ac1,200 (20% off) = \u20ac1,675 - \u20ac287.50 = **\u20ac1,387.50**",
